course: dictionary
lesson: 7074
title: Patron: helper, customer or saint
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A patron is a person who gives money or support to an artist, a charity or a group. In the past, kings and rich people were often patrons, because they paid artists to make paintings and books. When a sign says «Patrons only», it means customers only.
explain: Use the context to find which meaning fits. In «Saint Patrick is Ireland's patron saint», patron means a saint who looks after a country. Ask yourself: does my meaning make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The sentences here show three: a helper who pays, a customer, and a saint who protects. Patron is a noun, so it names a person, and patrons is the plural, for more than one person.
fact: A patron is a person who gives money or support to an artist, a charity or a group.
fact: A patron can also be a customer of a shop, restaurant or library.
fact: A patron saint is a saint believed to protect a country, a place or a group of people.
fact: «Saint Patrick is Ireland's patron saint.» Saint Patrick is the saint who looks after Ireland.
fact: Patron is a noun: a patron, patrons.
exercise: «Saint Patrick is Ireland's patron saint.» What does patron saint mean here? | A saint who sells books in a shop | *A saint believed to look after a country | A saint who paints pictures | A saint who is very old
exercise: A sign on the door says «Patrons only». Who is the sign for? | Only people who are very old | Only saints | *Customers of the shop or café | Only people who have never visited before
exercise: A rich lady pays a painter to make pictures for her. What is she? | *A patron of the painter | A librarian | A ticket seller | A saint of Ireland
test: In «The library's patron borrowed three books today», what does patron mean? | A saint who protects libraries | A book that is very old | A teacher who reads aloud | *A customer of the library
test: «St George is the patron saint of England.» What does this tell you? | He lives in England all his life | He is the king of England | *He is believed to look after England | He wrote a book about England
exam: Which sentence uses patron to mean a person who gives money to an artist? | The patron of the bakery bought two buns | The saint looked after the country | *The king was a patron who paid the painter to make a picture | St Patrick's Day is in March
